From: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PM / wakeup: avoid redundant s2idle_wake() calls in pm_system_wakeup()

Calling s2idle_wake() once when pm_abort_suspend transitions from 0 to 1
is sufficient to abort s2idle. Skip redundant wakeup kicks while an abort
is already pending.

Signed-off-by: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c b/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
index 79efb19..5600598 100644
--- a/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
@@ -941,8 +941,8 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_wakeup_pending);
 
 void pm_system_wakeup(void)
 {
-	atomic_inc(&pm_abort_suspend);
-	s2idle_wake();
+	if (atomic_inc_return_relaxed(&pm_abort_suspend) == 1)
+		s2idle_wake();
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_system_wakeup);
 
